# LC2 — semantic-merge conflict-time tripwire (PDR-049 / PDR-050).
#
# Memory and state files are concept-bearing narratives and indexes; git's
# default 3-way LINE merge silently corrupts their meaning (stacked entries,
# dropped sessions, split tables). Route conflicts on these surfaces to the
# `engraph-semantic-merge` driver, which FAILS LOUD and routes to the
# semantic-merge skill instead of producing a silent line-merge.
#
# The driver name is bound in git config (`merge.engraph-semantic-merge.driver`,
# not committable) by the agent-tools `postinstall` bootstrap. The registered
# command names the driver by its path within the checkout: git runs merge
# drivers from the top level of the checkout being merged, so one registration
# arms every worktree of the repository and each checkout runs its own build.
# A checkout whose `agent-tools/dist` is not built halts its merges on these
# paths with an unmerged file and a module-resolution error naming that path.
# Run `pnpm install` in that checkout (its postinstall builds and binds the
# driver), or `pnpm --filter @engraph/agent-tools build` when the checkout is
# already installed and only `dist` was cleaned. The command starts with
# `node`, so a client whose PATH has no `node` halts the same way. A fresh
# clone that has never run `pnpm install` has no binding and falls back to
# git's default merge, and a bare-repository or server-side merge never
# invokes any merge driver, so the human discipline in
# `.agent/skills/semantic-merge/SKILL-CANONICAL.md` remains the backstop.
.agent/memory/**/*.md merge=engraph-semantic-merge
